# CloudflarePurge

https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:CloudflarePurge

Fork of the upstream WMF extension with support for purging additional
hostnames (e.g. kiosk subdomains) alongside the canonical URL.

## Configuration

| Variable | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$wgCloudflarePurgeZoneID` | string | `""` | Cloudflare zone ID |
| `$wgCloudflarePurgeToken` | string | `""` | API token with Zone.Cache Purge permission (recommended) |
| `$wgCloudflarePurgeAuthEmail` | string | `""` | Legacy auth: account email |
| `$wgCloudflarePurgeAuthKey` | string | `""` | Legacy auth: global API key |
| `$wgCloudflarePurgeExtraHosts` | array | `[]` | Additional hostnames to purge (same path/query, different host) |

## Extra hosts

When `$wgCloudflarePurgeExtraHosts` is set, each page save or delete
purges the canonical URL plus one variant per extra host. All URLs are
sent in a single Cloudflare API call.

Example — purge both `www.kolzchut.org.il` and `kiosk.kolzchut.org.il`:

```php
$wgCloudflarePurgeExtraHosts = [ 'kiosk.kolzchut.org.il' ];
```

### API limit

Cloudflare's `purge_cache` endpoint accepts a maximum of **30 URLs per
request**. With 1 canonical URL + N extra hosts, you can have up to 29
extra hosts before hitting the limit. In practice this is not a concern
(1-2 extra hosts is the expected usage).
